  "note": "Hand-written D52 policy cases in milliseconds. heard arms the per-call latch. Unknown inventory is not zero. pcmLive means admitted browser/remote PCM, never the native microphone. transportAlive (default true) is false once the recording's audio transport has closed (EOF, error, or the app's PCM_STALE_AFTER = 45 s watchdog, measured from the last frame on that transport); pcmLive implies a live transport. A closed transport falls back at once, whatever the page state or count, and is not missing-page evidence: with the page present, control alive and a known positive count it arms no missing timer and no pageGone (D52.4 Q3), and restoring needs a live transport. A later zero count still runs callEnded. D52.5 (cases with resumeCapture:true, i.e. the hello listed resume-capture-v1; case callGeneration is the recording's selected generation): askResume means the app sends one resume-capture-v1 Start for this system/lost recording. It is emitted at the first tick with the audio transport closed, control alive, the page present (not navigating), the row present with a known positive count, the row's callGeneration equal to the recording's, and heard:true already seen on a row of that callGeneration. In these cases heard latches only on rows of the case callGeneration, so another call's heard never arms this recording's restore, OTHERS_GONE grace or ask. It is asked at most once per loss and control connection: controlConnection (default 0) identifies the current control connection and changes only with a new hello; resumeRefused:true marks the tick a resume was refused or failed and changes nothing (no retry on later ticks or on any timer, only on a new controlConnection). A restore or a fresh fallback starts a new loss. Cases without resumeCapture never ask. This is separate from the preserved legacy D33 vectors.",
